epics.observations:
The prototype implements an older prepayment model (catch-up Phases 09 and 15a): trigger is a procedure's billingRoute 'billableParty' plus patientPaymentCategory 'selfFundedPrepayment' with full|split detail; an office 'Raise pre-procedure invoice' button; amount is an estimate (feeFor with no contract) or a typed deposit; an ACCREC+ACCPAY pair whose payable is the List's anaesthetist and is released to them on receipt (xeroHandoff.ts:272, paymentActions.ts:99); and a balance invoice after authorise with a 'Less pre-payment deposit already invoiced' line (invoiceBuild.ts:385-391). The catalogue model is different throughout: Contract-flag trigger, fixed Contract line price (>0), optional admin approval, a letter, an AA Holding account, a holding-to-anaesthetist transfer at List authorise, credit note or refund on cancel, no further invoicing, no price override on a prepaid Contract, and a move that changes nothing.

Verifier corrections: FT-06.5 and US-06.5.1 changed from Missing to Contradicts, and US-06.5.3 from Partial to Contradicts, because the prototype implements wrong behaviour there (release of the payable to the anaesthetist before the procedure, estimate-priced re-prepayment). Genuinely Missing items are the letter (US-06.3.6), cancellation reversal (US-06.5.2) and the open-question story US-06.3.7. No item grades as Matches; the prototype only matches on small points (warning is never a block; move code re-triggers nothing; per-procedure scan; prepayment status is derived).

Closing the epic is one structural rework with a shared core: (1) a Contract prepaid flag and fixed-price line validation (US-04.2.14, US-04.3.2/3.4, US-05.4.2); (2) an AA Holding payee and a transfer entry in the ledger and Xero simulator (US-08.3.1, FT-09, FT-10.3, US-10.2.1); (3) credit note and refund primitives, which do not exist anywhere in the prototype (US-08.6.3, US-08.6.5, US-02.5.3); (4) an outgoing-invoice approval screen with a switch-off setting (does not exist; referenced by several other epics); (5) removal of the balance invoice and deposit deduction in the billing run (US-07.3.x, US-08.2.2, OQ-116 mixed Bookings); (6) the prepayment letter template (OQ-120) and the move email. Dropping the 'PHASE 41 SEAM' in listMoveActions.ts and slotActions.ts is part of it, since a move needs no payee repoint. Seed work: Fri 24 AM Riley ('prepayment', split $800 on $1,200, unpaid) and Fri 24 PM Nair ('prepaymentPaid', INV0001/BC0001 built in buildSeedBillingSlice) must be rebuilt on a prepaid Contract, with a PERSIST_VERSION bump. Demo guide beats S3 (money end to end) and S4 (prepayment warning, partial payment) change, a cancel-prepaid-booking beat fits S4, the S2 move line (03-demo-script.md:357) becomes true only after the rework, and the master demo guide HTML must follow. Open questions: OQ-119 (Contract changed after sent or paid), OQ-120 (does the invoice and letter name the anaesthetist), OQ-125 (what releases the holding account; the catalogue text uses office authorisation of the List, which the prototype should follow), OQ-97 (partial credit). Cross-epic item not owned here: the anaesthetist seeing the prepaid amount on the Booking (US-03.1.8); today only the office sees a fee."}
